  "description": "Standalone storage nodes for FluxFlow: blockified put/get/query/delete over an injected IStorageStore, with broadcast result/error/event ports. No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Storage",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T12:53:18.677Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "0OEBTT4SJTTSwOdjeFqbbyGGgEFtpUNwnX7fWTNUjFlCpfjh9hAEShHHNEDE5sbdZsDIp0QlHKsvXvXTD8+L6w==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 62067,
  "published": "2026-06-19T12:50:35.237Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt as standalone storage.put/get/query/delete nodes over an injected IStorageStore: request in, result broadcast out, failures on the error port, diagnostics on the event port. Every message travels as a FlowMessage<T> envelope so the correlation id flows request -> result (and onto the Found/NotFound and Records branches). The storage.store resource node and its connect/disconnect lifecycle are removed — the host owns the IStorageStore lifetime and injects the opened store into each node, exactly like the HTTP node over an HttpClient. The engine factory/module/registration/designer-metadata glue is removed; the nodes depend only on FluxFlow.Nodes and run without the engine. The IStorageStore contract, all request/result/record DTOs, options, error codes, and the store factory/lease/context types are unchanged, so the FileSystem and SqlFile adapters keep working.",
